                "evidence": "review changes_requested: The diff adds the recently-played network path in duetflow/spotify.py:148-167 even though spotify.py is in project.yaml's risky_set and operating_preamble.md says an autonomous task must not edit or change the behavior of any risky-set file. This task is declared autonomous in docs/ROADMAP.md, so the change violates the governing confinement contract and cannot merge until the endpoint change is provided through an allowed path or the task/contract is explicitly corrected.; duetflow/app.py:20-24 and 167-169 still route the public `duetflow collect` command to cmd_not_yet. Running `python3 -m duetflow.app collect` on this commit prints that Collection is not built and exits 2, so the phase-02 instruction to run Collection manually cannot store any plays.; duetflow/collector.py:18-40 never checks the elapsed gap against collection.max_collection_gap_minutes. Given a database whose newest play is more than 90 minutes old, Collection proceeds without any warning, hiding the roadmap-specified condition that more than Spotify's 50 available plays may already have been lost.; duetflow/collector.py:32 passes Spotify's millisecond `played_at` through models.to_iso(), which emits only whole seconds. For two events of the same track at 2026-01-01T10:00:00.100Z and 2026-01-01T10:00:00.900Z, collect reports and stores one row because both become 2026-01-01T10:00:00+00:00; the natural key therefore collapses a real Play and corrupts Current Rotation evidence.; duetflow/spotify.py:159-166 handles a 401 from GET /me/player/recently-played by immediately raising SpotifyError. With an expired access token, Collection aborts instead of refreshing the token once and retrying as docs/PLAN.md section 5 requires.; duetflow/spotify.py:159-166 handles a 429 by immediately raising SpotifyError and neither reads Retry-After nor distinguishes a QUOTA_EXCEEDED response. A rate-limited request followed by an available successful response therefore aborts rather than wai",
