                "evidence": "review changes_requested: duetflow/collector.py:36-44 measures collection.max_collection_gap_minutes from the newest stored Play instead of the last successful Collection, contrary to docs/PLAN.md section 8. Concrete wrong results: if Collections succeed at 12:00 and 13:00 but the user last played something at 08:00, the 13:00 run falsely warns and app.py records status 'warning'; if earlier Collections stored no Plays, last_play_at remains null and a later multi-hour missed-run gap produces no warning at all, silently defeating the loss detector.; duetflow/recent.py:32-85 performs the live Spotify HTTP request and owns 401 refresh retry plus 429/5xx retry behavior. A normal `duetflow collect` with no fake transport therefore reaches recent._get/urllib.request.urlopen outside spotify.py, violating docs/PLAN.md section 2 ('Only spotify.py performs network I/O') and section 5's requirement that this client behavior live in spotify.py. It also bypasses project.yaml's filename-based risky_set, which defines spotify.py as covering all Spotify network I/O, auth refresh, retry, and rate limits, so this safety-sensitive behavior can merge without the control intended for it; move it into spotify.py and subject that change to the required proof review.",
